      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the External Provider**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on an external provider to make the code concrete. I need to make a solid choice and integrate its specifics into the plan for the Python file. The file itself should be named `filter_metric_dimensions.py`.\n\n\n**Choosing the Provider & Structure**\n\nI've selected Google Cloud Monitoring and will use the `google-cloud-monitoring` library. The `filter_metric_dimensions.py` file will include a `filter_metric_dimensions` function. It takes `project_id`, `metric_type`, `resource_type`, `resource_labels`, and `interval_seconds` as arguments. I'm moving toward the code structure and will start creating the file.\n\n\n**Outlining the Python File**\n\nI'm now writing the Python file `filter_metric_dimensions.py` based on the chosen provider. The key structure includes a `filter_metric_dimensions` function. This function will take the necessary inputs: `project_id`, `metric_type`, `resource_type`, `resource_labels`, and `interval_seconds`. I'm starting to include the import and will specify metric and resource types to align with Google Cloud Monitoring. The data will be retrieved using the `ListTimeSeriesRequest`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863944832,
          "start": 1789863940051
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc344fd3001USCEnBad3FbTLj",
